-From 80ac3d4a0d4c6b4fa9861fdce112cbf74e1e7ad8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
-From: LocalLink Dev <dev@locallink.local>
-Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 09:56:19 +0000
-Subject: [PATCH] Admin console: browser dashboard over the admin API
-
-Replace the embedded /admin assets with a full console for monitoring and
-hardening pass on the admin API.
-
-Console (internal/httpapi/adminweb, served via go:embed):
-- 13 modules over the existing admin endpoints: overview dashboard, users,
-  devices, sessions, network, calls, transfers, security, audit, recovery,
-  diagnostics, settings, privacy.
-- Design tokens with light/dark themes, sidebar/shell, global search,
-  notification centre, identity menu, responsive 1240/1000/720 layout.
-- Charts drawn on canvas from the API's own series; no invented data, and
-  sections say so when an endpoint has nothing to report yet.
-- Permission-aware controls, session-expiry handling, skeletons, empty and
-  error states, inline SVG icons and system fonts only: no external assets,
-  so the console works on an isolated LAN.
-- Cache and hardening headers set per asset; extensionless paths fall back to
-  the shell while a missing asset stays a 404.
-
-Admin API:
-- Split the per-minute admin ceiling: anonymous probes keep the tight 30/min
-  brute-force cap in their own bucket, while credentialled console traffic
-  gets a 240/min budget. A console refresh reads eight endpoints and polls, so
-  the single blanket limit throttled ordinary use (reproduced by driving the
-  console in a browser).
-- The console surfaces a throttle to the operator, keeps the figures already on
-  screen and eases polling instead of replacing live data with error panels.
-
-Tests: 11 console guards (asset surface, MIME types, hardening headers, shell
-references, offline capability, endpoint registration, no placeholder data,
-escaping, overlay wiring, rate-limit handling) plus a rate-limit budget test.
-tools/console-render-check.mjs drives the served console in a headless DOM
-against a live server; it found the overlay and throttle defects above.
----
